{
  "summary": "Ensures that wallet replacement transactions generated by bumpfee do not have an nLockTime older than the transaction they replace. When creating a replacement, CCoinControl captures the original transaction's locktime as a minimum height floor for DiscourageFeeSniping. Random anti-fee-sniping backdating is then restricted between this minimum height and the current tip.",
  "problem": "Bitcoin Core's anti-fee-sniping logic randomly backdates transaction locktimes by 0 to 99 blocks approximately 10% of the time for privacy. During RBF fee bumps, this random roll can result in a replacement transaction having a lower locktime than the original transaction, creating an unnatural on-chain pattern that leaks a fingerprint identifying the transaction as originating from Bitcoin Core or Electrum.",
  "evidence": [
    "Closes issue #26526 ('bumpfee can decrease nLockTime').",
    "PR author mempool analysis of over 1,000,000 RBF transactions (2025-05 to 2026-06) found 200-300 backdated replacements per week (<2% of all replaced transactions): 'the few transactions that do exhibit backdating are easily fingerprintable as having been replaced using bumpfee in Bitcoin Core or Electrum.'"
  ],
