  "changed_since_previous": "Added comprehensive unit and functional test coverage for the minimum height boundary conditions and stale tip handling in DiscourageFeeSniping.",
  "card": "This pull request ensures wallet fee-bumped transactions do not receive an nLockTime earlier than the transaction they replace. Anti-fee-sniping randomly backdates transaction locktimes by up to 99 blocks roughly 10% of the time, which can cause bumpfee to produce replacements with older locktimes than the original. This regression forms an on-chain fingerprint identifying Bitcoin Core or Electrum fee-bumped transactions. An empirical survey cited in the PR detected 200 to 300 backdated replacements per week, representing under 2% of surveyed RBF transactions.",
